1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,932
Lucy, we really need to get working on this marketing assignment.

2
00:00:03,932 --> 00:00:07,434
We've only got five weeks left to the end of term to design it,

3
00:00:07,434 --> 00:00:08,326
carry it out,

4
00:00:08,326 --> 00:00:10,110
and then write up the results.

5
00:00:10,110 --> 00:00:10,160
Sure.

6
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,405
Well, let's get started right now.

7
00:00:12,405 --> 00:00:14,045
Let's go over the instructions.

8
00:00:14,045 --> 00:00:16,340
What exactly do we have to do?

9
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:20,578
Well, it says here we have to look at one area of the entertainment

10
00:00:20,578 --> 00:00:20,881
industry.

11
00:00:20,881 --> 00:00:23,000
There's a list of the different types.

12
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:23,740
What are they?

13
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:26,014
Music, cinema, theatre, sport,

14
00:00:26,014 --> 00:00:27,720
and eating out.

15
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:28,710
Is that all?

16
00:00:28,710 --> 00:00:29,760
Looks like it.

17
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:33,488
So we choose one branch of the industry and then we look at how

18
00:00:33,488 --> 00:00:35,351
two different groups of people use it?

19
00:00:35,351 --> 00:00:36,150
Is that right?

20
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:36,600
Yes.

21
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:41,150
And do we have to use any particular method to get our data?

22
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:43,250
Can we mail out a questionnaire,

23
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:44,650
or do face-to-face interviews,

24
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:46,050
or maybe even observations?

25
00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:49,206
Well actually, it looks like we don't have a choice.

26
00:00:49,206 --> 00:00:51,100
We have to do telephone interviews.

27
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:51,437
OK,

28
00:00:51,437 --> 00:00:56,160
so at least we don't have to waste time deciding between the different methods.

29
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:56,528
Yeah,

30
00:00:56,528 --> 00:00:57,263
that's right.

31
00:00:57,263 --> 00:00:57,631
Oh,

32
00:00:57,631 --> 00:01:00,940
and the other requirement is the number of interviewees.

33
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:03,269
Not too many, I hope.

34
00:01:03,269 --> 00:01:03,734
Ten?

35
00:01:03,734 --> 00:01:04,200
Twenty?

36
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,980
Well, we have to do two groups, remember,

37
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:11,150
and it looks like we have to interview fifteen for each group.

38
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:13,234
That's thirty altogether then.

39
00:01:13,234 --> 00:01:15,840
It's going to take ages.

40
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:16,133
Yes,

41
00:01:16,133 --> 00:01:18,185
but remember we're working on this together,

42
00:01:18,185 --> 00:01:20,530
so we'll only have to do fifteen each.

43
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:20,956
OK,

44
00:01:20,956 --> 00:01:23,510
so those are all the requirements?

45
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:25,430
Yes, looks like it.

46
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:26,106
So, first,

47
00:01:26,106 --> 00:01:28,470
which area are we going to choose?

48
00:01:28,470 --> 00:01:33,200
My preference would be cinema, since that's where I spend most of my money.

49
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:36,062
Hmm, I don't think that's such a good idea.

50
00:01:36,062 --> 00:01:39,559
I don't think there are huge differences in the market there.

51
00:01:39,559 --> 00:01:43,056
I mean you get young and old, male and female, rich

52
00:01:43,056 --> 00:01:45,600
and poor all going to the same movies.

53
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,956
Yeah, maybe you're right.

54
00:01:46,956 --> 00:01:48,650
Let's make it music then.

55
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:49,177
Right.

56
00:01:49,177 --> 00:01:53,920
So, what two groups will we compare and contrast?

57
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,670
Male and female?

58
00:01:55,670 --> 00:01:55,976
No.

59
00:01:55,976 --> 00:01:59,344
Most of my female friends like the same music as me.

60
00:01:59,344 --> 00:02:03,630
Different age groups would be much more likely to show up differences, I think.

61
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:06,213
Yeah, I suppose you're right again.

62
00:02:06,213 --> 00:02:08,796
I'll take some notes, shall I?

63
00:02:08,796 --> 00:02:09,226
So...

64
00:02:09,226 --> 00:02:10,088
Age Groups.

65
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:10,518
Well.

66
00:02:10,518 --> 00:02:12,240
What do you think?

67
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:15,254
Maybe twenty-five or under for one group,

68
00:02:15,254 --> 00:02:18,698
and forty-five or over for the other group?

69
00:02:18,698 --> 00:02:20,850
That should show up differences.

70
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:21,540
Right.

71
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:21,907
OK.

72
00:02:21,907 --> 00:02:22,274
Next.

73
00:02:22,274 --> 00:02:26,680
How about the kind of music they like-let's give them some choices

74
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:29,250
and then we can just tick boxes.

75
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:29,908
OK.

76
00:02:29,908 --> 00:02:34,514
Let's have pop, jazz, folk, easy listening...

77
00:02:34,514 --> 00:02:35,830
What else?

78
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:37,780
Well, we should include classical.

79
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:40,120
Some people like it, you know.

80
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:40,537
OK.

81
00:02:40,537 --> 00:02:40,953
OK.

82
00:02:40,953 --> 00:02:45,120
And then we should have how they listen to music.

83
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,173
The medium.

84
00:02:46,173 --> 00:02:46,700
Right.

85
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:51,440
Let's include radio, CD-and then I guess there's TV.

86
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:52,350
What about concerts?

87
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:54,170
You know, in pubs and halls.

88
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:56,600
Oh yeah, we should include live music of course.

89
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,319
OK, we're on a roll now!

90
00:02:58,319 --> 00:03:01,470
Next point could be about where they actually get their music.

91
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:04,647
You mean like, do they buy it in music shops,

92
00:03:04,647 --> 00:03:05,600
or department stores?

93
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:05,880
Yes,

94
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:07,560
or download it from the Internet.

95
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:07,874
Right.

96
00:03:07,874 --> 00:03:09,760
That could be for recorded music.

97
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:12,274
Then we need another section for live music.

98
00:03:12,274 --> 00:03:14,160
Where do they go for that?

99
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:14,632
OK.

100
00:03:14,632 --> 00:03:17,940
Let's say disco, pub, club, concert hall...

101
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,094
Or opera house!

102
00:03:19,094 --> 00:03:22,170
And I guess we should include karaoke bars.

103
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:23,630
Not many of them in this city!

104
00:03:23,630 --> 00:03:24,003
OK.

105
00:03:24,003 --> 00:03:25,866
We'll leave that out then.

106
00:03:25,866 --> 00:03:27,730
So, what's left to do?

107
00:03:27,730 --> 00:03:28,482
That's it.

108
00:03:28,482 --> 00:03:32,240
Well, now we can make a time-scale for doing it.
